			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#732">GUILD RULES AND GOALS/IDEALS:</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							To become a membership you must be season 10+ and a wood or high elve follower of Tunare (exceptions possible). You may ask or be asked to join before season 10, but not fully accepted into membership, untill actually attaining your 10th season.<br />
<br />
<br />
GUILD RULES<br />
<br />
1.The most important duty for all members of this guild is to uphold the guild's ideals and values. These are loyality, nobility, justness, honesty, compassion, respect. These should be what is already of yourself, and also always what is shared and shown to all other guild members, as well as all others outside the guild that you may encounter along they way. Also, though should not need to be mentioned, all general game rules and commonly accepted practices (such as matters pertaining to killstealing, campstealing, Etc.), themselves, are to be followed at all times, as well as any and all guild rules. Your behavior should and will always reflect what is about you, and the guild itself, all at the same time.<br />
<br />
2. There will be a member limit or cap of not more than 50 at any one time. This allows for there to be, depending on attendance, up to 6-8 full groups, enough for any raid situations that the guild may plan. Also, a larger guild can have the tendancy to get out of conrtol, and lax in it's goals, responsibilites, and behavior. The limit is something which should help to avoid that from happening. Should all go well, and remain stable into the future, there is always the possibility that the limit can be amended to allow for a higher membership total.<br />
<br />
3. We are to be a roleplay guild, and members, will be encouraged to do so always, as much as possible. This should be evident already, from the makeup of the guilds races, as it is. This also applies to grouping, in regards to those of evil aligned races/classes, and their hunting habits. This applies to such things as the hunting of good aligned NPC's, city guards, etc. At no time should any memeber be engaged in such activities. While it would be most desireable to forbid grouping with evil races/classes, it is not always practical, and will be allowed (provided the above activities are not being conducted), allthough to avoid doing so whenever possible would be more desireable. <br />
<br />
4. Disputes/Disipline. While it would be in everyone's best interests to never have to have a need for such a topic, almost always at some point, it becomes necessary, and unavoidable. The guidelines for this will remain very simple. First, always, we would hope that those in dispute would be able to resolve their differences calmly and amongst themselves in an appropiate and mutually acceptable manner. However, should it not be possible, then certain steps will be followed. This is to also apply to any occurances where some form of discipline may or would be required. In straight forward fashion, guild officers/advisors are to investigate any such matters, to their fullest extent, then bring them to the attention of the guild's leaders, who will then find the best way to resolve the issue at hand. As these situations can vary greatly, no one set outcome can be pre-determined. The guilds leaders will look into the matter thouroughly, and then decide the best, fairest course of action. This pertains to disciplinary measures, as well, such as fines, demotion, repayment, disbandment, Etc. Decisions made by the guilds leaders will be the fairest possible, and also final. <br />
<br />
5. Officers: Positions will be made and filled by leadership decision, and the number determined by guild population, and need. Those that are selected, will be expected to continue to do that which got them there. Tose selected, will be expected to continue to do that which got them there.<br />
<br />
THE GUILD'S GOAL(S): <br />
<br />
What we would have for goals, what we would want to see happen, both in the beginning, and as we travel together into the future is really very simple. In actuality, there is only one real goal, and that is what is written in the Charter, itself. All esle that could be described or listed as goals, are really just the ways to go about making the guild to be that which it is being created to do, become and live as a family. Treat each other as a family, care about each other as a family, help each other as a family, do things as a family. To always try to do so, can only bring pride and honor to yourself and the guild, yourself and the family, help it to grow to be the best it can be...<br />
<br />
There are many ways to go about making that happen. Some will be shown here, others, in the future, in the form of ideas and thoughts we and any others may have, which will always be welcome to be heard. By helping to help each other, as well as any others, is how it brings everyone closer together and makes everything possible. Some ways to do this, are very simple. Think what you would want to have, and what you would want to do. Then think the same way of the others. There, you will find the way...<br />
<br />
Help each other do things, get things, accomplish things. And if someone does this for you, be sure to do the same in return, when you can, wether right away, or at a better time. Though the exact ways will always vary, these are just some general ways and ideas as how it should be... <br />
<br />
Think of your guild, your family, first. If you have something you don't need, give it to a member who does, or may. Or give it to the guild, to hold for when someone comes along that may, or to trade for something else that would be better, either for you, or another. Perhaps if you do, the guild may have something that can be of use for you, too. Or will in the future. If something is of greater value, and you wish to sell it, there is nothing wrong with that. Everyone also needs money. Just try to offer it to a memeber for less than you would a stranger. Perhaps will be a time where someone knows where to get a certain item, but can't do it on their own, but with help, they can. As a guild, and a family, it should happen these ways, always. Both from you, and if so, in return also. It's one way to help yourself, and each other become better and closer as time goes on. And this should also apply to others outside, or of another good guild, as well, when possible. By doing so, you'll make friends and allies, for both yourself, and the guild. We would always welcome new friends, or allies, perhaps even lead to an alliance with another guild, too, if they are of the same standards. wether for Trade, for needed items and such, or strength, in times of need or war, for it is also our duty to fight to keep the evil from our lands, and those that would hunt our guards, raid our cities. Is but another thing we would like to see happen, and can, easily, if everyone helps to make that happen. And can only make us stronger...<br />
<br />
Also, there are all sorts of other ways that can be to help each other, and it should be these that are done, whenever possible. We would like to have times and events where we can do exactly that. Wether it be to have a guild picnic with smaller events, such as races and dueling contests, or guild created quests. And from time to time, an organized raid, or practices to get the guild trained for an actual raid. Some have to and will be arranged by the guild as a whole and it's leaders. And some can be done by just a few. Get together to train languages, or train others to hunt and fight. Help make groups to hunt, when possible. Help another find one if they need. If you can't, for some reason, at the time, maybe you know a friend who can. And many other ways are there too, these are but a few. Even a small guesture can be a big help at times...<br />
<br />
In all, the purpose and goal, in the end, is to make the guild a family of pride and honor, the strongest, the closest it can be. These are just some ways that will help to make that happen along the way. There is nothing wrong with wanting and doing things for yourself, too. Just remember, for ever how much you help those in the guild, and the guild as awhole, the more they will help you, too...<br />
<br />
And &quot;that&quot; is what it's all about.
						</td>
					</tr>
