						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#731">Like what you see? STOP! (And just be sure...)</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							...You are of the sort that would like to become and stay a member of a guild such as this, both now, and into the future. This is to be a strong, family type guild. NOT a pure raiding, power-leveling &quot;uber&quot; guild. *SEE http://www.eqclanx.com/clanxdilemma.htm for an example of what this is about. That does not mean, both paths cannot be followed, as time goes on, and we grow, become stronger. It is the differences in &quot;how&quot; we go about that, along the way. As a Family guild first and always, that will also try to do some of the same things in due time, provided it is done, as a Family. We have outlined all this already, in the most pleasant, appealing way possible, to this point, as we show you that which has been our dream and our goal. For some, though, it could be a bit misleading, or non-specific. This part is to address just that. In simple, direct terms. Time for the brass tacks, so to speak...<br />
<br />
LEADERSHIP/OFFICERS (Command Structure):<br />
<br />
- First and foremost, and to use a favorite qoute to describe it...There can be only one. period. And that's all there will be. Temra and myself are the leaders, and will have final say, including veto power, rule amendments, Etc., for any and all guild matters that may warrant such measures. Simply to ensure that the guild stay true to it's design. Any and all decisions and actions that need or require such action will always be made in the best possible interests of the guild, as a whole, and in the fairest way possible. And also the firmest. There can be no long term stability without this. It is that simple.<br />
<br />
- Advisors/officers: will be selected by the leadership, from those that show the most willingness to help and be involved with the guild. Though few at first, as we grow, and our needs aswell, so will the number of openings. All of which will be handled in the same manner. Once named to a position, it will be that person's added responsibility to be sure to remain to do that which got them there, in the first place. Quite simply, should the individual's desire fade away once named to a position, they will find that position will fade away too.<br />
<br />
- Advisors: will be 3 to start, with the possibility for more, as we grow in size, as mentioned above. It will be their main duty to help oversee and handle guild matters, in the same fashion as it's leaders. They answer only to the guild's leaders, which they are to do, at all times, for any and all matters that would be of importance or affect the guild as a whole, for final approval. This mostly pertains to matters more serious in nature, such as disputes, disbandments, amendments and/or changes in the guild's policy's, and any instances where a solution cannot be reached otherwise. In the abscence of both guild leaders, the advisors will act in their place, until their retun. The guild leaders will, however, always have the right to overturn or amend any actions taken by the Advisors, should it be deemed necessary, allthough unlikely. They will also be responsible for hearing and seeing to any matters that a guild Officer should bring to their attention. Quite simply, the advisors are to be ones that are of sound, clear, and like minds, able to reason and make decisions on their own, with the best interests of the guild and it's members in mind, as well as just plain common sense, and keep all true to it's original course. The leaders will be the ones to watch and see that this happens, always.<br />
<br />
- Officers: These positions will be more geared towards each and any of the guild's needs, as they arise. Such examples would be for recruiting, guild trade and alliance liasons, member training and group coordination and leadership during raids, Etc., as well as any other instances that may arise, that would warrant a position for it. They will be subordinates to the Advisors, and report to them immediatley, any matters of importance that should arise, but also be able to handle trivial matters on their own. They, as well as the advisors, will always be responsible to help and guide members as best they can, and also to keep track of the general member's concerns, ideas, requests, Etc., and then report them to the Advisors, or the guild leaders.<br />
<br />
- Members: Are expected to act and conduct themselves in the best interests and views of the guild. While the proper respect should always be shown to all guild officers, Advisors, leaders, Etc., all members are also encouraged to speak their mind, and voice any concerns, requests, ideas, etc. Just do so in an appropiate, proper fashion. We are your guild, and therefore, also your family, and always will what is important to you, be important to all the rest of us as a whole.<br />
<br />
RULES &amp; GOALS: Some Specifics...<br />
<br />
- What has been outlined already is pretty straight forward, and what will be expected from the guild and it's members. It is the guild's purpose, in general. The guild is made up of people, and it is the people that make the guild. Follow always these guidlines, and the charter itself, and we will succeed in our purpose. It is that simple.<br />
<br />
- Should an instance arise where a member is found to be acting or conducting themselves in a manner that would reflect poorly upon the guild, and it's ideals, measures can and WILL be taken, to deal with this, as already outlined, as well as any other way deemed necessary, depending on the situation. As friends and family, with exception for perhaps the most serious instances where disbandment or immediate disiplinary action taken, a warning would first be issued to the member in question. We would hope that should be enough to correct any problems of this nature, and it should be just that simple among family and friends. But, if not, stronger measures will then be taken.<br />
<br />
- As much as it should be that everyone try to help each other, a little common sense must also prevail at times, too. All that means, in simple terms, is the guild cannot do every single thing for you, and some sense of self-reliability, should also prevail. As examples, it should be not to feel, that just because this is a family guild, and there could be a Druid or Cleric as members, that does not make them automatically your own personal Rezzer, or means of transportation, and be expected to drop everything always should you call. If you need help, and someone can, they surely will help you, as you should try to do in return. Just keep in mind, others are here to have fun, too, and will at times have things they wish or need to do of their own. Even the leaders, at times. Always feel free to ask, and more than not, you should have them help you need, as soon as it can happen. Like all else, though, just have and use common sense for these things.<br />
<br />
- As mentioned before, this is to be a family guild, not a pure raiding-type guild. We are here to have fun, make friends, help each other, and do things together, just as you would as a family. If you are just looking to amass items and wealth by any means necessary, and look to join a guild for only those reasons, then you've come to the wrong place, and should seek another guild. That is not intended to be mean or harsh, but only show quite clearly it is not what this, to us, is all about. Though maybe not quite so fast or easily, all those things can still be had and done. As we grow, raids and groups can and will become more common, trained for, arranged, if enough should wish to make them happen. If everyone works together, in time everything can be done. And done by and with those that would be your friends and family, together, and help them to all have the same too, and have fun, along the way. But that is, in the end, up to you. The guild will be only what you help and choose to make it. That too, is just that simple.<br />
<br />
AND AFTERWARDS:<br />
<br />
Now that you have seen the rest, is time for you to decide that which you would want to have for aguild to be a member of, and what type. If what we are all about is what you want, and is right for you, and you right for us, then feel free to contact us and let us know you wish to join us and our family. It is yet another thing,<br />
that can be so very simple...
